tests/fm-procevent.test.sh at BASE commit 355f46fe5528ccc9790481171bf9da48dee2e90d
(target's tests/fm-procevent.test.sh copied on top so the new regression case
is present), run unmodified on this macOS host where $TMPDIR sits under
/var -> /private/var:

  $ bash tests/fm-procevent.test.sh

ok - no configured source means no generated state and no process
not ok - reconcile never claimed the registered source
EXIT:1

The suite dies at the second assertion -- an ordinary, pre-existing claim
(no symlink-specific test reached yet) -- because on macOS the whole temp
tree used by the test harness is reached through a symlinked ancestor, and
the base guard (`fm_procevent_private_directory_valid`, comparing physical
location against a purely lexical path normalization) rejects every such
directory. This matches the reported symptom: "Two test suites ... could
not run on macOS at all: red at base on unmodified files."
